    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate on 2026-09-10, the Zurich Zebras lean heavily on the top-tier profiles of **Junior Caminero** (76.09) and **Trea Turner** (75.77). **Junior Caminero** is the strongest play of the day, benefiting from an favorable matchup against P\u00e9rez, M (4.75 xERA) and an optimal #3 spot in the order. Meanwhile, **Trea Turner** remains our premier asset in the SB category; he receives a significant boost due to his matchup against Javier, who possesses a slow delivery that increases **Trea Turner**'s already high probability of swiping bags. **Yordan Alvarez** (62.98) rounds out the high-leverage starts, maintaining a strong rating despite facing the elite arm of Wheeler (3.24 xERA), largely buoyed by his elite 0.447 xwOBA and platoon advantage.\n\nWhile **Chase Meidroth** (40.24) secures the final spot in our lineup, his projection is marginal, suffering from a lower spot in the order (#7) and a neutral matchup against Jones. The benching decisions were largely dictated by schedule availability, as **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Christian Yelich**, **Caleb Durbin**, and **Kazuma Okamoto** are all inactive due to team off-days. With no other viable options currently active, we are forced to weather the risk of **Chase Meidroth**\u2019s lower efficiency to maintain our game caps. We continue to monitor the status of our depth pieces\u2014including **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, **Colt Keith**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Carson Benge**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez**\u2014for any late-breaking lineup changes that might necessitate a substitution to avoid sub-40 performance floors.",
